  "content": {
    "id": "p3-q9-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "9",
    "prompt": "Find an example of two polynomials $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ for which",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p3-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\deg(P+Q)=\\deg(P(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For example, $P(x)=x^2$ and $Q(x)=x$.",
          "worked": "Choose $P(x)=x^2$ and $Q(x)=x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(P+Q)(x)&=x^2+x\\\\\\deg(P+Q)&=2\\\\\\deg(P)&=2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\deg(P+Q)=\\deg(P)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\deg(P+Q)<\\deg(P(x))$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For example, $P(x)=x$ and $Q(x)=-x+1$.",
          "worked": "Choose $P(x)=x$ and $Q(x)=-x+1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(P+Q)(x)&=x+(-x+1)\\\\(P+Q)(x)&=1\\\\\\deg(P+Q)&=0\\\\\\deg(P)&=1\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $\\deg(P+Q)<\\deg(P)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\deg(P+Q)<\\deg(P-Q)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For example, $P(x)=x^2$ and $Q(x)=-x^2-x$.",
          "worked": "Choose $P(x)=x^2$ and $Q(x)=-x^2-x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(P+Q)(x)&=x^2+(-x^2-x)\\\\(P+Q)(x)&=-x\\\\(P-Q)(x)&=x^2-(-x^2-x)\\\\(P-Q)(x)&=2x^2+x\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore $\\deg(P+Q)=1<2=\\deg(P-Q)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 34
      }
    ]
  },
